- op: discuss  # 2d22
  at: '2026-09-19T21:57:30Z'  # 2d22
  by: agent  # 2d22
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2d22
  clock: 3  # 2d22
  nonce: 2d22  # 2d22
  message: "Satisfied, with a before/after measurement on this repository's own survey.\n\nTHE STATEMENT held because the field had no absent value. `Symbol.is_exported` is now `Optional[bool] = None`, and only a positive input fills it:\n- an analyzer's own rule writes True or False and is believed;\n- an export modifier (`pub` / `public` / `exported` / `pub(...)`) fills True;\n- a language signal that the symbol is not public at all fills False in finalize, because public-API membership needs public visibility (INV-jusot) and `compute_visibility` returns public for the DEFAULT, so a non-public level is always somebody's observation;\n- nothing else fills it.\n\nTHE ROOT CAUSE named both halves, and both are fixed. The fold `is_exported or is_exported_from_modifiers(modifiers)` existed in TWO copies — `cli.py::_classify_symbols` and `sketch.py::_run_analysis` — and each resolved every unobserved record to False. Both now upgrade only on the modifier's PRESENCE. The finalize visibility downgrade is kept as-is and is now the only writer of a negative that no analyzer supplied, which is correct: it fires only on a real signal.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE — `hypergumbo survey .` on this repository, before and after, compared per record id (51,795 records present in both):\n- `false` -> `null`: **28,049**\n- `false` -> `false`: 7,902 (real measurements, kept)\n- `true` -> `true`: 15,844\n- **no `true` was lost, and nothing moved to `false` that was not already there.**\nTotals: before 16,069 true / 36,659 false / 0 null; after 16,079 true / 8,018 false / 28,654 null.\nBy kind, what moved: 23,466 `method` (py.py has a rule for module-level constructs, not for methods — filed as WI-kohah), 2,049 `external_symbol`, 1,890 `file` anchors, 270 `call_site`, 222 `function`. By language: 26,467 python, 355 bash, 287 language-less, 255 rust, 195 yaml, 179 markdown, 120 toml, 50 typescript.\n\nALSO FIXED, because the audit found it two-sided: the JS/TS analyzer marked only the exported and left the rest to the default. A module's `export` clauses ARE the whole of its public API, so a declaration absent from them is now MEASURED as not exported — including in a file with no exports at all, which is a measurement that nothing is exported, not an absence of one. The synthetic per-file anchor is left undecided, since the field is about declarations and this analyzer has no rule for the anchor.\n\nUNIT EVIDENCE, mutation-checked (three mutants, each killed with a real `passed|failed` line): restoring the `or` fold in `cli.py` (3 failed), restoring it in `sketch.py` (1 failed), and reading an absent key as False in `from_dict` (2 failed). The new test module pins the record's own default, an explicit False surviving serialization, an absent key reading as unknown, and end to end: a bash function (no rule anywhere) is `null`, a Python `__all__` member is `true`, a non-member is `false`, and a `_private` is `false`.\n\nA CONSEQUENCE INSIDE ADR-0057, worth naming because it retired machinery that landed hours earlier: `ABSTENTION_BLIND_ATTRIBUTES` is DERIVED from `Symbol`'s field defaults, and `is_exported` was its last member. The set is now empty, every anchored producer rules `observes=()`, and INV-huboz's declaration goes dormant — the field itself abstains, per record, which is what I argued was the better mechanism when scoping that row. The declaration stays armed: a tracked attribute that gains a concrete default repopulates the set the day it lands and the registry contract test refuses every producer that has not re-ruled. Because an empty live set would make that guard untestable, `abstention_blind_attributes()` is now a function over a record type and is exercised on one that HAS such a field.\n\nSCHEMA: 0.20.11 -> 0.20.12, `supply_chain.is_exported` widens from `boolean` to `boolean|null` (generator and `docs/schema.json` regenerated, spec §Symbol and §9 updated). Readers that test truthiness are unaffected — all of them do.\n\nFILED, not swept in: WI-kohah (py.py has no exportedness rule for methods; the 23,466 records above are honest now but still unmeasured)."  # 2d22
